    "That said, there's a common thread across most hotel-lobby scenting at this level of hospitality, Marriott included: warm rather than cold, welcoming rather than edgy, and restrained enough to run for hours without becoming fatiguing. Think amber, vanilla, soft woods — comforting notes rather than bold, statement ones. That's the general profile most people are actually chasing when they say they want the Marriott smell.",
